// Title: DLL Load via LSASS
// Sigma ID: b3503044-60ce-4bf4-bbcb-e3db98788823
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-10-16 | Modified: 2022-04-21
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, execution, persistence, T1547.008
// Description: Detects a method to load DLL via LSASS process using an undocumented Registry key
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://blog.xpnsec.com/exploring-mimikatz-part-1/
//   - https://twitter.com/SBousseaden/status/1183745981189427200
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_event_susp_lsass_dll_load.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey contains "\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\NTDS\\DirectoryServiceExtPt" or RegistryKey contains "\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\NTDS\\LsaDbExtPt") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\system32\\lsass.exe" and (RegistryValueData in~ ("%%systemroot%%\\system32\\ntdsa.dll", "%%systemroot%%\\system32\\lsadb.dll")))))
